### Log in through the gateway (public route; forwarded to auth-service unchanged).
### Stores the tokens for the requests below. Synthetic account only.
POST http://localhost:4004/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dr.example@pms.test",
  "password": "<password>"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
  client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### Protected route: the gateway verifies the token, removes Authorization and forwards the
### verified identity (X-User-Id, X-User-Roles, X-Patient-Id for PATIENT) to patient-service.
GET http://localhost:4004/api/v1/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Without a token: 401 problem+json from the gateway; patient-service is never called.
GET http://localhost:4004/api/v1/patients

### Spoofed identity headers are stripped: patient-service only sees the verified values.
GET http://localhost:4004/api/v1/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-User-Roles: ADMIN
X-User-Id: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000099

### Unrouted path: fail closed (401 without a token, 403 with a valid one), not 404.
GET http://localhost:4004/not-a-route
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Gateway probes (public). Readiness does not depend on the downstream services.
GET http://localhost:4004/actuator/health/readiness

###
